# a borrowed typedef is a second name for its source, and the source must be
# exactly the base, as it must for an owned one. A `ListVal u8` borrowed as a
# `Name` (a typedef over String) was accepted and read as a String in the C.
Name: typedef String
main: function is {
    v: ListVal u8
    n: Name v.borrow
    print "\{n.count}"
}
